    {
      "id": "86af5605-64f5-4543-bb1f-20ce465ea432",
      "phaseId": "99d19246-1ba9-4720-9895-e70c66acf144",
      "number": 346,
      "shortId": "E9UYL",
      "priority": 19,
      "shortName": "fixed-value-sets-become-types",
      "title": "Fixed value sets become types, so a misspelt one cannot compile",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "# The hole\n\nSeveral properties accept only a fixed set of words. In a description they are written as free text:\n\n```rust\n.prop(\"orientation\", PropValue::Text(\"vertcal\".into()))   // typo — compiles, silently ignored\n```\n\nThe separator stays horizontal and nothing reports anything. This is the same silent failure\nF003/P010/T006 spent a whole task removing from **actions** (a misspelt argument name did nothing\nforever, one stderr line in debug and none in release). It is still live in the **UI vocabulary**.\n\nThree value sets already have types in `heca-view` for exactly this reason — `ViewSize`,\n`ViewVariant`, `ViewAlign`. The rest never got them.\n\n# ✅ DECIDED BY THE USER 2026-07-27\n\n**Give the small sets real types, and generate the glyph list.** Two separate answers because the\nglyph set is not like the others.\n\n## The small sets — measured, `heca-grid-ui`\n\n| grid-ui type | Values | Used by |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Orientation` (`widgets/separator.rs`) | Horizontal, Vertical | Separator.orientation |\n| `ScrollAxes` (`widgets/scroll_region.rs`) | Vertical, Horizontal, Both | Scroll.axes |\n| `ToastSeverity` (`widgets/toast.rs`) | Info, Success, Warning, Danger | Toast.severity |\n| `AlertVariant` (`widgets/alert.rs`) | Info, Success, Warning, Danger | Alert.variant |\n| `LabelSide` (`widgets/checkbox.rs`) | Right, Left | Checkbox.label_side |\n| `ActiveMarker` (`widgets/item.rs`) | None, Bar, Check | Row.marker, Item.marker |\n| `TextAlign` (`scene.rs`) | Start, Center, End | Label.align |\n\n**`AlertVariant` and `ToastSeverity` have identical values** — one mirror (`ViewSeverity`) serves\nboth. So **six** new types, 21 values in total.\n\n## ⚠️ They must NOT get `PropValue` variants\n\nThis is the lesson from F003/P011/T018, and it is the whole reason this task is small.\n\n`PropValue` already carries three hardcoded mirrors (`Size`, `Variant`, `Align`) — the closed shape\n`Map` was added to escape. **A fixed value set travels as its name**, so `PropValue::Text` carries\nany of them and the *type* lives in the authoring layer. Give each mirror\n`impl From<ViewOrientation> for PropValue` producing `Text(name)`, so `.prop(\"orientation\",\nViewOrientation::Vertical)` reads well without `PropValue` learning anything.\n\nVerified this works end to end: `prop_to_json` turns `Text` into a JSON string and the widget's own\nenum deserializes from its snake_case name (`heca-view-realize/src/lib.rs:222`); `prop_to_input`\nturns it into `PropInput::Text` and the generated `set_prop` parses the name\n(`:299`). No realize change should be needed — confirm rather than assume.\n\nCollapsing the existing three into this scheme is a wire-format change and wants its own task.\n\n## Glyphs — generated, not copied\n\n`Glyph` (`heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/icon.rs:33`) has **52 variants and grows**. A hand-written mirror\nis the \"list nobody is forced to update\" that this codebase keeps being bitten by.\n\nPlan:\n1. `Glyph::ALL` + a `name()` in `heca-grid-ui`, mirroring the `WidgetKind::ALL` pattern the model\n   already uses. Useful on its own.\n2. A **checked-in generated** `ViewGlyph` in `heca-view` — `heca-view` cannot depend on\n   `heca-grid-ui` and must not start.\n3. A drift test in **`heca-view-realize`** (the one crate that sees both) comparing `ViewGlyph`'s\n   list against `Glyph::ALL` and failing when they diverge, naming what is missing. Same\n   fails-closed shape as `prop_drift.rs`.\n\n# Steps\n\n1. Six mirrors in `heca-view`, serde `rename_all = \"snake_case\"`, each with `name()` and\n   `From<_> for PropValue` → `Text`.\n2. Confirm a realized widget actually receives each one (a test per mirror, asserting on the widget,\n   not on the parse).\n3. `Glyph::ALL` + `name()` in `heca-grid-ui`; generated `ViewGlyph` in `heca-view`; drift test in\n   `heca-view-realize`.\n4. Point the existing docs at the types where they currently show text values.\n\n# Acceptance\n\n- A misspelt value in any of the seven sets **does not compile** when written through a mirror.\n- `heca-view` still depends on nothing but serde.\n- The glyph list cannot silently disagree with `heca-grid-ui`'s.\n- Whole workspace green, clippy 0 warnings.\n- Unblocks F003/P011/T006, whose builders can then be honestly typed.\n\n---\n**Completion summary:**\n# ✅ DONE 2026-07-27 — commit `1653169`\n\nSix mirrors in `heca-view`: `ViewOrientation`, `ViewScrollAxes`, `ViewSeverity`, `ViewLabelSide`,\n`ViewMarker`, `ViewTextAlign`. Six not seven because `ToastSeverity` and `AlertVariant` carry the\nsame four values, and two copies of one list is how this codebase gets into trouble. A seventh,\n**`ViewJustify`**, was added later in `7183250` — T019's inventory came from the widgets' own\nproperties and `justify` is a `Layout` field, so it never appeared.\n\n**None of them has a `PropValue` variant, and the comment there says the next one must not either.**\nA fixed set travels as its name, so `Text` carries every one of them and the type belongs in the\nauthoring layer. `Size`/`Variant`/`Align` predate that rule and are the closed shape `PropValue::Map`\nwas added to escape.\n\n**Glyphs are generated, then held to account.** 52 names and growing, so `ViewGlyph` is generated and\n`every_glyph_name_has_a_mirror` (`heca-view-realize`) compares it against the library's own list both\nways, naming what is missing. Verified by deleting a glyph and reading the failure:\n`these glyphs exist in heca-grid-ui but not in ViewGlyph … [\"backspace\"]`. Nothing was needed in\n`heca-grid-ui` — `Glyph::ALL` and the `PropName` derive already existed.\n\n**Two guards on the names**, because agreement across two crates and a serde attribute is not\nsomething to assume: `name()` and the serde spelling must match (checked over a list generated from\nthe same variants, so it cannot miss one), and every mirror is taken through `PropValue` into a\nrealized widget and asserted to change it — matching names is not the same as the name being\nunderstood.\n\nDocs: `docs/widgets.md` examples now use the types; `docs/chrome-and-ui.md` §R2 records the rule.\n\nNothing visual changed, so there was nothing for the user to look at; the proof is the tests.",
      "notes": "",
      "statusLog": [],
      "decisions": [],
      "acceptedDecisions": [],
      "checklist": [],
      "subtasks": [],
      "dependsOn": [],
